## Requirement Summary (from client, 2026-11-12) 

- All standard templates follow the SAP brand — one theme, many events 
- Templates use UDEX as the design reference 
- Owners pick a template and change content and images only — NOT colours, fonts or layout rules 
- Header and footer are locked; more locked areas to follow from business rules 
- Block-library owner is a designer (to be named) with a process like sap.com's 
- Designs and template governance still to be agreed with the business 
- One gap identified: a page can switch off or replace the header/footer through page metadata (`header: off`) — locking the fragment isn't enough; event pages need a code guard 

