### Header/Footer Guard (COMPLETED ✅)
Problem: EDS honours header: off metadata on any page — including event pages. Locking the fragment files is not enough.

Solution: Added guardEventPageLayout() to scripts/scripts.js:

function guardEventPageLayout() {
  const path = window.location.pathname;
  const isEventPage = path.startsWith('/events/');
  if (!isEventPage) return;

  const metaTags = document.querySelectorAll('meta[name="header"], meta[name="footer"]');
  metaTags.forEach((meta) => {
    const name = meta.getAttribute('name');
    const value = meta.getAttribute('content')?.trim().toLowerCase();
    if (value === 'off' || value === '') {
      console.warn(`[Guard] Blocked attempt to set "${name}: ${value}" on event page ${path}`);
      meta.remove();
    }
  });
}

// Run immediately before EDS processes meta tags
guardEventPageLayout();
Test page: events/test-event/index.html

Has header: off and footer: off in metadata
Guard successfully blocks both — header and footer remain visible ✅
Console warning confirmed ✅
Key learning: EDS converts .metadata block to <meta> tags before scripts run — guard must check <meta> tags, not .metadata divs.

